                    <!-- Process & Design Choices Deep Dive -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-950/80 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
                        <h5 class="text-sm font-mono font-bold text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2">
                          <span>💡</span> The Design "Why": Friction Over Signage
                        </h5>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                          Most sustainability campaigns rely on static informational posters that people ignore during routine disposal. For international students and newcomers, navigating distinct municipal streams (landfill vs. organics vs. co-mingled recycling) creates decision fatigue.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                          We designed EchoBin to introduce <strong class="text-slate-200">physical and conversational friction</strong>. By locking the lid and verbally calling out mistakes with a sassy persona, the bin forces conscious re-evaluation. Humor was chosen deliberately: it disarms defensiveness and makes environmental correction an entertaining social moment rather than a sterile reprimand.
                        </p>
                      </div>
                      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-950/80 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
                        <h5 class="text-sm font-mono font-bold text-cyan-400 uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2">
                          <span>⚡</span> The Engineering "Process": Pipeline Concurrency
                        </h5>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                          Migrating from laptop mockups to a headless Raspberry Pi introduced severe interaction latency. Our initial prototype processed steps synchronously in a linear blocking waterfall:
                        </p>
                        <div class="p-2 rounded bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 font-mono text-[10px] text-rose-400">
                          Audio Listen → Vision Inference → Text Generation → Audio Playback (&gt;4s lag)
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                          This delay destroyed the conversational rhythm. We resolved this by refactoring into a <strong class="text-slate-200">multi-threaded, queue-based architecture</strong>. Audio listening, Gemma vision classification, and ElevenLabs speech generation run concurrently in non-blocking worker threads.
                        </p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

